now to our exclusive interview with  Salvatore Sam and nello the grand father  accused of negligent homicide and the  death of his granddaughter Chloe Wiegand  the 18-month old fell 150 feet from a  Royal Caribbean cruise ship docked in  Puerto Rico and nella was holding the  girl up against what he thought was a  bank of closed windows when she slipped  from his grasp lead national  correspondent David beg no sat down with  an L o in his first interview since the  incident David how is he handling this  Anthony he seemed emotionally numb when  we met him yesterday he told us the  reason he wanted to do this interview  was to try and plead with Royal  Caribbean cruise line to put signs up  when and where they actually have  windows open on the ship we wanted to do  the interview  to better understand exactly what  happened this grandfather is facing  three years in prison because  prosecutors believe his actions on the  ship were reckless the process by which  he slipped how did that happen oh I know  I was trying to reach the glass and I  know that we leaned over they try to  have her reach the glass and that point  she's left  but at that moment did you realize there  was no glass I didn't realize there  wasn't any glass till the absolutely  dude was too late I mean even when she  first fell I thought she fell in front  of me  I thought she fell in front of me what  was your reaction when you found out  that you were the subject of this  criminal investigation Chloe being gone  is the worst thing ever so I'm like  whatever you know  I don't know what to help me understand  what you mean there's nothing worse that  they can do to me and what's already  happened we are gonna have more of our  exclusive interview with Salvatore  Salmonella in our next half hour he's  gonna talk about the health condition he  says he has that may have played a role  in the tragedy plus we have new details  about that surveillance video which  shows the final moments leading up to  what happened well so difficult the  details and none of it changes the fact  that I feel like three years is a lot to  put on top of somebody who's already  suffering yeah David thank you very much
 

